" Colour compound attributes (data-*, aria-*, class:*) as a whole. `data`,
" `prompt` and `class` are htmlArg keywords, and a keyword always wins over a
" match at the same start column — so `data-my-tooltip-prompt` renders in three
" colours and `class:active` in two. Matching from the separator dodges the
" keyword. An after/syntax file cannot do this: lazy.nvim drops ~/.vim/after
" from the runtimepath.
augroup compoundHtmlAttrs
  autocmd!
  autocmd Syntax html,svelte
        \ syn match htmlArg "\%([0-9A-Za-z]\)\@<=\%([-:][-.:0-9_A-Za-z]\+\)\+"
        \ contained containedin=htmlTag
augroup END

